# #1099 Stage 3: HTML mode in QuickMail's compose window. The same steps run against the new
# editor (UseNewEditor = on) and the current WPF rich editor (off). A new message is open, with
# focus in the To box.
w 4
q +{TAB}
w 2
q {TAB}
w 3

# 0. Into the body, and into HTML mode.
k %y
w 3
e Message body
k ^+3
w 5
e Switched to HTML mode

# 1. Typed-word echo: each word as Space ends it, and the last as Enter ends it.
t one two the cup toast three
w 3
e one
e two
e the
e cup
e toast
k {ENTER}
w 3
e three

# The rest of the text, typed without logging.
Q Alpha line
q {ENTER}
q {ENTER}
Q Beta line
q {ENTER}
Q Gamma
q {ENTER}
Q A much longer line of text here
q {ENTER}
Q Short
w 3

# 2. Down from the top: each line once, a blank line as blank.
k ^{HOME}
w 3
e one two the cup toast three
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Alpha line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e blank
e! Beta
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Beta line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Gamma

# 3. From the end of a long line, Down onto a shorter one: that line alone.
k {DOWN}
w 3
e A much longer line of text here
k {END}
w 2
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Short

# 4. Ctrl+Up by paragraph.
k ^{UP}
w 3
k ^{UP}
w 3
e A much longer line of text here
k ^{UP}
w 3
e Gamma

# 5. A heading: the command says what it did, and the line reads as its text.
k ^%2
w 4
e Heading 2
k {UP}
w 3
e Beta line
k {DOWN}
w 3
e Gamma

# 6. Bold, typed.
k ^{END}
w 2
q {ENTER}
k ^b
w 3
e Bold on
t strong words
w 3
e strong
k ^b
w 3
e Bold off

# 7. A list.
q {ENTER}
k ^+l
w 3
e Bullet list on
t first item
w 2
k {ENTER}
w 3
t second item
w 2
k {UP}
w 3
e first item
k {DOWN}
w 3
e second item

# 8. The formatting where the caret is.
k ^t
w 5
e Bullet list item

# 9. Leaving and coming back.
k %u
w 3
e Subject
k %y
w 3
e Message body
